From 3c3538f9f91d0b4ce267ded4cdcc6dd7fad4de27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 14 May 2026 14:10:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dos: Phase 11 patch 0060 -- Cirrus 5434 chip-driven BLT
 helper (wave-49)

Exposes the Cirrus CL-GD5434 BLT engine's NORMAL screen-to-screen rect
copy mode (BLT_MODE 0x00, ROP SRCCOPY) so NXEngine-evo's FG tilemap
render can replace ~1881 per-flush sysmem-memcpys with chip-driven
VRAM-to-VRAM rect copies. Engine-side integration (sprite/tileset
relocation to off-screen VRAM at load time + per-tile BLTCopy calls)
ships separately in nx-engine's lane; this patch is the SDL-side
primitive only.

Two new public APIs in include/SDL3/SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h:

  bool SDL_DOSVesaDirect_IsCirrusBLTAvailable(void);
  bool SDL_DOSVesaDirect_BLTCopy(Uint32 src_vram_off, Uint32 dst_vram_off,
                                  int w, int h, int src_pitch, int dst_pitch);

Probe anchor: tests/probes/bltpat-v2.c (Phase 11 wave-38 ride-along) which
validated the Cirrus 5434 BLT engine's PATTERN_COPY mode at 68 MB/s on
actual g2k Pentium OverDrive 83 MHz + Cirrus CL-GD5434 + UNIVBE 6.70.
The wave-49 helper uses NORMAL mode (0x00) rather than PATTERN_COPY (0x40)
because the engine needs arbitrary rect copy, not 8x8 pattern tiling --
but the rest of the register-programming sequence is identical to the
probe's proven path (GR[0x20-0x33] layout; BLT_RESET pre-programming
per V_PAT_C anchor; SRCCOPY ROP).

Chip-presence detection (one-time, cached, lazy):

  - Killswitch first: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_CIRRUS_BLT=0 (strict-"0") forces
    availability=false regardless of chip detection. Strict-match per
    CLAUDE.md DOSKUTSU env-var convention.
  - Unlock Cirrus extension registers: SR[0x06]=0x12.
  - Read CRTC[0x27] for chip-rev. STRICT 5434-only detection (CRTC[0x27]
    == 0xA8). Other Cirrus variants (5430=0xA0 / 5436=0xAC / 5446=0xB8)
    AND non-Cirrus chips fall through to availability=false. Engine
    must use its software-blit fallback when availability is false.
  - Clear GR[0x0B] bits 1 + 4 per bltpat-v2 errata (screen-to-screen
    BLT constraints).

Per-call BLT sequence:

  - GR[0x31]=0x04 -- BLT_RESET pre-programming clears stale state.
  - Spin busy-bit clear (capped 200k iters ~ 10 ms on PODP83).
  - Program BLT registers GR[0x20-0x33]: width-1, height-1, dst_pitch,
    src_pitch, dst_offset (24-bit), src_offset (24-bit), no transparency
    (0x2F=0), NORMAL mode (0x30=0x00), SRCCOPY ROP (0x32=0x0D).
  - GR[0x31]=0x02 -- kick the BLT engine.
  - Spin busy-bit clear (same cap). On timeout, emergency-reset chip
    and return false so engine falls back to software blit.

Return-false paths:

  - Availability off (chip not 5434, killswitch engaged).
  - Out-of-range params (w/h <= 0 or > 4096; non-positive pitches).
  - Chip stuck busy on pre-flight or post-kick poll.

Engine must handle false return by falling back to its existing
software _blit_indexed primitive. The chip state is left in a clean
(post-reset) state on the timeout path so the next call starts fresh.

doskutsu_dbg_log banners (smoke-gate two-witness pattern):

  - "sdl: wave-49 Cirrus BLTCopy: ENABLED (Cirrus 5434 detected; ...)"
    on successful chip detection.
  - "sdl: wave-49 Cirrus BLTCopy: DISABLED (chip not Cirrus 5434; ...)"
    on non-5434 fallback.
  - "sdl: wave-49 Cirrus BLTCopy: DISABLED (killswitch ...)"
    on killswitch.
  - "sdl: wave-49 Cirrus BLTCopy: first BLT success (src_off=... ...)"
    on first successful BLT (one-time gate so the smoke can verify the
    runtime path is exercised, not just the literals embedded).

Per CLAUDE.md sec. Critical Rules:
  - Strict-match env-var per DOSKUTSU convention.
  - ASCII-only source text.
  - DOS-PORT: tag is not used here -- this is SDL3-DOS-backend-native
    code, not port glue. The "DOSKUTSU patch 0060" block comment is
    the equivalent attribution.

No coupling with the existing direct-VESA fast path
(SDL_DOSVesaDirectPresentFull / GetState / BankedFlush) -- the BLT
engine writes to VRAM independently. Engine code that mixes BLT-driven
tile rendering with dosmemput-based present must ensure CPU writes
complete before chip BLT reads its source; on single-threaded DOS this
is automatic for sequential calls.

Workspace-local patch (per sdl_ai_policy memory + this repo's
vendor/SDL/CLAUDE.md notice: SDL upstream forbids AI-authored code;
patches live in patches/SDL/ and are never contributed back).

Modifies:
  include/SDL3/SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h  (new API declarations)
  src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c       (new API implementations)

Engine-side integration + smoke-gate BANNERS array update + docs/
internal/BOOT.md entry live in the parent doskutsu repo (not in this
vendor commit).
---
 include/SDL3/SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h | 129 ++++++++++++++
 src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c      | 223 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 352 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h
index 034bedf74..528f1e7f0 100644
--- a/include/SDL3/SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h
+++ b/include/SDL3/SDL_dosvesa_directaccess.h
@@ -504,6 +504,135 @@ extern SDL_DECLSPEC void SDLCALL SDL_DOSVesaDirectProgramPalette(const SDL_Palet
 extern SDL_DECLSPEC bool SDLCALL SDL_DOSVesaDirectPresentFull(const SDL_DOSVesaDirectState *st,
                                                                const void *pixels);
 
+/* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * Cirrus 5434 chip-driven BLT engine helper (patch SDL/0060, wave-49)
+ * ------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ *
+ * Exposes the Cirrus CL-GD5434 BLT engine's NORMAL (screen-to-screen
+ * linear) rect-copy mode. Used by engines that have already staged
+ * source pixel data into off-screen VRAM (sprite/tileset atlas) and
+ * want to replace per-tile system-RAM memcpys with chip-driven
+ * VRAM-to-VRAM rect copies.
+ *
+ * Anchor: tests/probes/bltpat-v2.c (wave-38 ride-along) validated the
+ * Cirrus PATTERN_COPY mode at 68 MB/s on actual g2k Pentium OverDrive
+ * 83 MHz + Cirrus CL-GD5434 + UNIVBE 6.70. This helper uses NORMAL mode
+ * (BLT_MODE 0x00) for arbitrary rect copy rather than 8x8 PATTERN_COPY
+ * mode (0x40), but the same chip-side register sequence + BLT_RESET
+ * pre-programming applies. The Cirrus 5434 chip-rev anchor is
+ * CRTC[0x27] = 0xA8 (other Cirrus variants are NOT engaged by this
+ * helper -- 5430/5436/5446 fall through to the "available=false" path
+ * because the BLT register layout differs subtly across the family).
+ *
+ * Engine-side contract:
+ *   1. Detect availability ONCE at startup via
+ *      SDL_DOSVesaDirect_IsCirrusBLTAvailable(). If false, use the
+ *      existing SDL_memcpy/dosmemput fallback path.
+ *   2. At sprite/tileset load time, push pixel data to an off-screen
+ *      VRAM region (>= vram_pitch * vram_h bytes past the visible
+ *      framebuffer) via SDL_DOSVesaDirectBankedFlush(). The engine
+ *      manages off-screen VRAM allocation; SDL does NOT track it.
+ *   3. Per-tile: call SDL_DOSVesaDirect_BLTCopy(src_vram_off,
+ *      dst_vram_off, w, h, src_pitch, dst_pitch). Returns true on
+ *      success; false means the BLT engine errored (e.g. chip stuck
+ *      busy on the kick poll). On false, engine must fall back to
+ *      software blit for that tile and may retry the next flip.
+ *
+ * Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_CIRRUS_BLT=0 (strict-"0") forces
+ * "available=false" regardless of chip detection. Default = ON when
+ * Cirrus 5434 is detected. Any other value (including unset or "1")
+ * uses the default-ON behavior.
+ *
+ * No coupling with the existing direct-VESA fast path -- the BLT
+ * engine writes to VRAM independently of the dosmemput/LFB-memcpy
+ * path used by SDL_DOSVesaDirectPresentFull. Engine code that mixes
+ * the two MUST issue a flush of any pending VRAM write before the
+ * BLT engine reads its source, but this is the engine's
+ * responsibility (the chip doesn't see partial CPU writes from a
+ * separate execution context -- DOS is single-threaded).
+ */
+
+/**
+ * Returns true if the Cirrus 5434 BLT engine is available for use via
+ * SDL_DOSVesaDirect_BLTCopy().
+ *
+ * On first call: probes CRTC[0x27] for chip rev 0xA8 (Cirrus 5434),
+ * clears the screen-to-screen BLT constraints in GR[0x0B], and caches
+ * the result. Also emits a one-time `doskutsu_dbg_log` banner narrating
+ * either ENABLED (chip detected) or DISABLED (with reason: chip not
+ * Cirrus 5434, or killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_CIRRUS_BLT=0). On
+ * subsequent calls returns the cached result without re-probing.
+ *
+ * Safe to call before any window is created (the probe only touches
+ * VGA Sequencer / CRTC / Graphics Controller indexed ports).
+ *
+ * \returns true if the BLT engine is available; false if the chip is
+ *          not a Cirrus 5434 or the killswitch is engaged.
+ *
+ * \threadsafety Single-threaded.
+ *
+ * \since This function is available since SDL 3.2.0 (DOSKUTSU patch 0060).
+ *
+ * \sa SDL_DOSVesaDirect_BLTCopy
+ */
+extern SDL_DECLSPEC bool SDLCALL SDL_DOSVesaDirect_IsCirrusBLTAvailable(void);
+
+/**
+ * Chip-driven VRAM-to-VRAM rectangular copy via the Cirrus 5434 BLT
+ * engine (NORMAL mode, BLT_MODE 0x00, ROP SRCCOPY).
+ *
+ * Both source and destination MUST be in VRAM (no system-RAM source
+ * allowed -- the chip BLT engine reads only from VRAM). The engine is
+ * responsible for staging source pixel data into off-screen VRAM at
+ * load time via SDL_DOSVesaDirectBankedFlush() (or equivalent) before
+ * calling this helper.
+ *
+ * Issues BLT_RESET (GR[0x31]=0x04) before programming the rect copy
+ * to clear any stale BLT state per the wave-38 V_PAT_C probe anchor.
+ * After programming the BLT registers (0x20-0x33), kicks the engine
+ * via GR[0x31]=0x02 and polls busy bit 0x08 with a capped iteration
+ * count (~200k) so a stuck chip can't hang the caller.
+ *
+ * Width and height registers are 12-bit on Cirrus 5434, so the
+ * maximum rect dimensions are 4096 x 4096. The function returns
+ * false (with no chip state mutation) for out-of-range or non-positive
+ * dimensions.
+ *
+ * On the FIRST successful BLT, emits a one-time `doskutsu_dbg_log`
+ * banner narrating the src/dst offsets and rect size so the smoke
+ * gate can verify the path is actually exercised (two-witness pattern
+ * per CLAUDE.md sec. Build verification).
+ *
+ * \param src_vram_off byte offset into VRAM of the source rect's
+ *                     top-left corner. Engine manages off-screen
+ *                     VRAM addressing.
+ * \param dst_vram_off byte offset into VRAM of the destination rect's
+ *                     top-left corner.
+ * \param w rect width in pixels (1..4096). At 8bpp this is also bytes.
+ * \param h rect height in pixels (1..4096).
+ * \param src_pitch source-stride in bytes per row (typically the
+ *                  off-screen atlas's pitch).
+ * \param dst_pitch destination-stride in bytes per row (typically
+ *                  vram_pitch from SDL_DOSVesaDirectGetState).
+ * \returns true if the BLT completed; false if availability is off,
+ *          parameters are out of range, or the BLT engine errored
+ *          (timeout on busy poll). On false the engine should fall
+ *          back to its software-blit path for this tile.
+ *
+ * \threadsafety Single-threaded.
+ *
+ * \since This function is available since SDL 3.2.0 (DOSKUTSU patch 0060).
+ *
+ * \sa SDL_DOSVesaDirect_IsCirrusBLTAvailable
+ * \sa SDL_DOSVesaDirectBankedFlush
+ */
+extern SDL_DECLSPEC bool SDLCALL SDL_DOSVesaDirect_BLTCopy(Uint32 src_vram_off,
+                                                             Uint32 dst_vram_off,
+                                                             int w,
+                                                             int h,
+                                                             int src_pitch,
+                                                             int dst_pitch);
+
 /* Ends C function definitions when using C++ */
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
diff --git a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c
index 1ee59c1e5..8fdc0fa00 100644
--- a/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c
+++ b/src/video/dos/SDL_dosframebuffer.c
@@ -2606,4 +2606,227 @@ bool SDL_DOSVesaDirectPresentFull(const SDL_DOSVesaDirectState *st,
     return true;
 }
 
+// ============================================================================
+// DOSKUTSU patch 0060 (Phase 11 wave-49) -- Cirrus 5434 chip-driven BLT helper.
+//
+// Exposes the Cirrus CL-GD5434 BLT engine's NORMAL screen-to-screen rect
+// copy (BLT_MODE 0x00, ROP SRCCOPY) for engines that have staged source
+// pixel data into off-screen VRAM. Replaces ~1881 per-flush sysmem memcpys
+// in NXEngine-evo's FG tilemap render with chip-driven VRAM-to-VRAM
+// rect copies. Probe anchor: tests/probes/bltpat-v2.c (wave-38) which
+// validated PATTERN_COPY at 68 MB/s on actual g2k. NORMAL mode uses the
+// same chip-side register sequence + the V_PAT_C BLT_RESET anchor; the
+// only mode-bit difference is GR[0x30]=0x00 here vs 0x40 in the probe.
+//
+// Strict Cirrus 5434 detection (CRTC[0x27] == 0xA8). Other Cirrus
+// variants (5430/5436/5446) fall through to availability=false because
+// the BLT register layout differs subtly across the family. Non-Cirrus
+// VESA chips also fall through. Engine must check availability and use
+// its software-blit fallback when this returns false.
+//
+// Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_CIRRUS_BLT=0 (strict-"0") disables.
+// Default: ON when Cirrus 5434 detected.
+//
+// Workspace-local patch; never upstreamed (per sdl_ai_policy memory).
+// ============================================================================
+
+// VGA / Cirrus extended-register port macros. Same constants as
+// tests/probes/bltpat-v2.c (the probe that validated this register
+// sequence on real g2k). VGA_DAC_* are already defined elsewhere in
+// this file; the Cirrus extended-register set is added here.
+#define CIRRUS_SR_INDEX  0x3C4
+#define CIRRUS_SR_DATA   0x3C5
+#define CIRRUS_GR_INDEX  0x3CE
+#define CIRRUS_GR_DATA   0x3CF
+#define CIRRUS_CRTC_IDX  0x3D4
+#define CIRRUS_CRTC_DATA 0x3D5
+
+// Tri-state availability cache. -1 = not yet probed; 0 = unavailable
+// (chip not 5434, or killswitch engaged); 1 = available. Single-
+// threaded backend -> no atomic needed.
+static int _cirrus_blt_available = -1;
+
+// One-time first-success banner gate. Bumped to 1 the first time
+// SDL_DOSVesaDirect_BLTCopy returns true so the smoke gate can verify
+// the path is exercised (two-witness pattern per CLAUDE.md).
+static int _cirrus_blt_first_success_logged = 0;
+
+// Probe + cache chip availability. Called lazily from
+// SDL_DOSVesaDirect_IsCirrusBLTAvailable and SDL_DOSVesaDirect_BLTCopy.
+// Emits a one-time doskutsu_dbg_log banner narrating the verdict.
+static int _cirrus_blt_check_availability(void)
+{
+    if (_cirrus_blt_available >= 0) {
+        return _cirrus_blt_available;
+    }
+
+    // Killswitch first -- if env is strict "0", skip chip probe entirely.
+    // Strict-match per CLAUDE.md DOSKUTSU env-var convention: only the
+    // literal string "0" disables. Unset or any other value uses the
+    // default-ON behavior.
+    const char *env = SDL_getenv("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_CIRRUS_BLT");
+    if (env && env[0] == '0' && env[1] == 0) {
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("sdl: wave-49 Cirrus BLTCopy: DISABLED "
+                         "(killswitch SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_CIRRUS_BLT=0)");
+        _cirrus_blt_available = 0;
+        return 0;
+    }
+
+    // Unlock Cirrus extension registers. SR[0x06]=0x12 -- canonical Cirrus
+    // unlock sequence. On non-Cirrus chips the SR readback won't match.
+    outportb(CIRRUS_SR_INDEX, 0x06);
+    outportb(CIRRUS_SR_DATA, 0x12);
+    outportb(CIRRUS_SR_INDEX, 0x06);
+    Uint8 sr06_rd = inportb(CIRRUS_SR_DATA);
+
+    // Read CRTC[0x27] for chip-rev identification.
+    outportb(CIRRUS_CRTC_IDX, 0x27);
+    Uint8 crtc27 = inportb(CIRRUS_CRTC_DATA);
+
+    if (crtc27 != 0xA8) {
+        // Strict 5434-only detection per the patch contract.
+        // Other Cirrus variants (5430=0xA0 / 5436=0xAC / 5446=0xB8)
+        // fall through to availability=false. Non-Cirrus also lands here.
+        doskutsu_dbg_log("sdl: wave-49 Cirrus BLTCopy: DISABLED "
+                         "(chip not Cirrus 5434; CRTC[0x27]=0x%02X "
+                         "sr06_rd=0x%02X; engine uses sysmem fallback)",
+                         (unsigned)crtc27, (unsigned)sr06_rd);
+        _cirrus_blt_available = 0;
+        return 0;
+    }
+
+    // Cirrus 5434 detected. Clear screen-to-screen BLT constraints
+    // in GR[0x0B] bits 1 + 4 per the bltpat-v2 probe errata.
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x0B);
+    Uint8 gr0b = inportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA);
+    gr0b &= (Uint8)~((1u << 1) | (1u << 4));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x0B);
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, gr0b);
+
+    doskutsu_dbg_log("sdl: wave-49 Cirrus BLTCopy: ENABLED "
+                     "(Cirrus 5434 detected; CRTC[0x27]=0xA8; "
+                     "GR[0x0B] screen-to-screen constraints cleared; "
+                     "engine may call SDL_DOSVesaDirect_BLTCopy)");
+    _cirrus_blt_available = 1;
+    return 1;
+}
+
+bool SDL_DOSVesaDirect_IsCirrusBLTAvailable(void)
+{
+    return _cirrus_blt_check_availability() != 0;
+}
+
+bool SDL_DOSVesaDirect_BLTCopy(Uint32 src_vram_off,
+                                Uint32 dst_vram_off,
+                                int w,
+                                int h,
+                                int src_pitch,
+                                int dst_pitch)
+{
+    if (_cirrus_blt_check_availability() == 0) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    if (w <= 0 || h <= 0 || src_pitch <= 0 || dst_pitch <= 0) {
+        return false;
+    }
+    // Cirrus 5434 BLT width/height registers are 12-bit (max 4096).
+    if (w > 4096 || h > 4096) {
+        return false;
+    }
+
+    // BLT_RESET pre-programming per V_PAT_C anchor (bltpat-v2 line 488-
+    // 493). Clears any stale BLT state from a prior op so the new
+    // programming starts from a known-idle baseline.
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x31);
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, 0x04);
+
+    // Spin until chip is idle (busy bit GR[0x31] bit 0x08 clear).
+    // Capped iteration count so a stuck chip can't hang the caller --
+    // ~200k iterations is roughly 10 ms on PODP83 worst-case, which is
+    // far longer than a successful BLT (~1 ms for 320x240).
+    {
+        int idle = 0;
+        for (int spin = 0; spin < 200000; spin++) {
+            outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x31);
+            if ((inportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA) & 0x08) == 0) {
+                idle = 1;
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+        if (!idle) {
+            // Chip is stuck even after BLT_RESET. Mark this BLT as
+            // failed; engine falls back to software blit. The chip
+            // state may or may not recover for the next call; we
+            // don't auto-disable the helper because a transient stick
+            // shouldn't permanently kill the path.
+            return false;
+        }
+    }
+
+    // Program BLT registers. Same layout as bltpat-v2's blt_program_pattern
+    // EXCEPT GR[0x30]=0x00 (NORMAL screen-to-screen mode) instead of
+    // 0x40 (PATTERN_COPY mode). This is the only mode-bit difference;
+    // the rest of the register sequence is identical to the probe's
+    // proven path. ROP 0x0D = SRCCOPY (same as probe).
+    const Uint16 w_m1 = (Uint16)(w - 1);
+    const Uint16 h_m1 = (Uint16)(h - 1);
+
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x20); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)(w_m1 & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x21); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)((w_m1 >> 8) & 0x0F));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x22); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)(h_m1 & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x23); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)((h_m1 >> 8) & 0x0F));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x24); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)(dst_pitch & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x25); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)((dst_pitch >> 8) & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x26); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)(src_pitch & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x27); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)((src_pitch >> 8) & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x28); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)(dst_vram_off & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x29); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)((dst_vram_off >> 8) & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x2A); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)((dst_vram_off >> 16) & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x2C); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)(src_vram_off & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x2D); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)((src_vram_off >> 8) & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x2E); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, (Uint8)((src_vram_off >> 16) & 0xFF));
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x2F); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, 0x00); // no transparency
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x30); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, 0x00); // NORMAL screen-to-screen mode
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x32); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, 0x0D); // SRCCOPY ROP
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x33); outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, 0x00); // no extension flags
+
+    // Kick the BLT engine: GR[0x31]=0x02 starts the operation.
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x31);
+    outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, 0x02);
+
+    // Spin until busy bit clears (BLT complete). Same iteration cap as
+    // the pre-flight idle check. 320x240 at 68 MB/s -> ~1 ms; cap is
+    // way longer so stuck-chip path falls through cleanly.
+    int idle = 0;
+    for (int spin = 0; spin < 200000; spin++) {
+        outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x31);
+        if ((inportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA) & 0x08) == 0) {
+            idle = 1;
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+    if (!idle) {
+        // BLT did not complete within the budget. Emergency-reset
+        // the chip so the NEXT call starts clean, then return false
+        // so the engine falls back to software.
+        outportb(CIRRUS_GR_INDEX, 0x31);
+        outportb(CIRRUS_GR_DATA, 0x04);
+        return false;
+    }
+
+    // First-success banner: emit once for the smoke gate's
+    // two-witness pattern. Subsequent successful BLTs are silent
+    // (no per-call log spam in the hot path).
+    if (!_cirrus_blt_first_success_logged) {
+        _cirrus_blt_first_success_logged = 1;
